{card:whatisaqrcode}
image:"%%"
{widgets}
button1:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[442,312],"script":"whatisaqrcode.0","text":"Next","style":"rect"}
button2:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[10,312],"script":"whatisaqrcode.0","text":"Prev","style":"rect"}
title:{"type":"field","size":[492,17],"pos":[10,22],"locked":1,"font":"menu","show":"invert","border":1,"align":"center","value":"What is a QR Code?"}
button3:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[78,312],"script":"whatisaqrcode.0","text":"Index","style":"rect"}
field1:{"type":"field","size":[248,238],"pos":[254,48],"locked":1,"border":0,"value":{"text":["QR (Quick-Response) codes are two-dimensional barcodes invented by Masahiro Hara in 1994. Today they are a common method of representing hyperlinks in the physical world, and most cell phones with cameras can scan and decode them.\n\nThe \"qr\" module can generate images of QR codes. It is particularly useful in combination with ","the \"pdf\" module",", which is often used to produce printable versions of decks, zines, or greeting cards.\n\nThis module was developed by referencing Kang Seonghoon's public-domain QR code generation library, ","qr.js",", with many simplifications and adaptations to suit Lil and its standard library."],"font":["","","","",""],"arg":["","https://beyondloom.com/decker/pdf.html","","https://github.com/lifthrasiir/qr.js",""]}}

{script:whatisaqrcode.0}
on click do
 t.Prev:"SlideRight"
 t.Next:"SlideLeft"
 t.Index:"BoxOut"
 go[me.text t[me.text] 15]
end
{end}

{card:terminology}
{widgets}
button1:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[442,312],"script":"whatisaqrcode.0","text":"Next","style":"rect"}
button2:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[10,312],"script":"whatisaqrcode.0","text":"Prev","style":"rect"}
title:{"type":"field","size":[492,17],"pos":[10,22],"locked":1,"font":"menu","show":"invert","border":1,"align":"center","value":"Terminology"}
button3:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[78,312],"script":"whatisaqrcode.0","text":"Index","style":"rect"}
field1:{"type":"field","size":[248,238],"pos":[254,48],"locked":1,"border":0,"value":"QR codes come in \"versions\" indicating their size and data capacity. These range between 1 and 40. Higher numbers are larger codes.\n\nData in a QR code is encoded as one ofseveral \"modes\", which can be \"numeric\" (digits 0-9), \"alphanumeric\" (see left), \"octets\" (arbitrary sequences of 8-bit values), or \"kanji\" (which is not supported by this module). More general modes take up more space.\n\nQR codes support error-correction to compensate for obscured or illegible pixels when reading a code. The \"ecclevel\" can be set to \"L\", \"M\", \"Q\", or \"H\", with escalating ability to correct errors and corresponding decrease in data capacity.\n\nThe data in a QR code is XORed with a \"mask\" pattern between 0 and 7; QR encoders select masks according to various heuristics intended to minimize patterns which may confuse decoders."}
field2:{"type":"field","size":[195,25],"pos":[34,76],"locked":1,"border":0,"align":"center","value":"valid characters in the \"alphanumeric\" encoding, which can represent many URLs:"}
field3:{"type":"field","size":[161,40],"pos":[51,108],"style":"code","value":"0123456789\nABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ\n $%*+-./:"}

{card:qr_generate}
{widgets}
button1:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[442,312],"script":"whatisaqrcode.0","text":"Next","style":"rect"}
button2:{"type":"button","size":[60,20],"pos":[10,312],"script":"whatisaqrcode.0","text":"Prev","style":"rect"}
title:{"type":"field","size":[492,17],"pos":[10,22],"locked":1,"font":"menu","show":"invert","border":1,"align":"center","value":"qr.generate[]"}
